## 9. Information Growth

A major requirement for useful intelligence is actual information acquisition.

The system therefore distinguishes:

```text
Representational capacity
```

from:

```text
Acquired information
```

Actual information enters through:

```text
observation
interaction
measurement
learning
external storage
computation
```

The system begins with a relatively compact structure:

```text
S0
```

and accumulates materialized information:

```text
S0
 ↓
S1
 ↓
S2
 ↓
S3
 ↓
...
```

The hyperoperation structure describes the much larger space in which these states may exist.

Thus:

```text
Compact generative structure
        +
acquired information
        +
selectively materialized states
```

forms the working knowledge system.

