## 10. Memory Model

A possible memory hierarchy:

```text
Level 1
Physical / explicit memory

Level 2
Compressed learned representations

Level 3
Symbolic and recursive structures

Level 4
Generative rules

Level 5
Hyperoperation-defined possibility spaces
```

Only a fraction of higher-level structures need to be materialized at any moment.

Materialized results may be cached and subsequently become part of explicit memory.

